flowchart TD
    A([Start: Select the right GitHub Copilot offering])

    A -->|Start by understanding where the customer is today| B{What stage is the customer in?}

    B -->|Still exploring or just getting started| C[Innovation and Exploration]
    B -->|Already using Copilot and building capability| D[Skilling and Adoption]
    B -->|Scaling usage or optimizing impact| E[Scale, Governance and Optimization]

    C -->|Let’s understand current exposure| C1{Have teams used Copilot before?}

    C1 -->|No or very limited exposure across teams| C2[Zero to Agents Immersion]
    C2 -->|Help teams get familiar and build confidence| C2A[Build baseline awareness and confidence]

    C1 -->|Some awareness but limited hands-on usage| C3[GitHub Copilot Hackathon]
    C3 -->|Create shared team experience and momentum| C3A[Create hands-on team experience and momentum]

    D -->|What is the main gap today?| D1{What is the main adoption need?}

    D1 -->|Developers are using Copilot but not consistently| D2[GitHub Copilot for Developers Intermediate]
    D2 -->|Standardize usage and improve effectiveness| D2A[Improve prompt engineering secure coding and best practices]

    D1 -->|Teams want to expand beyond coding into workflows| D3[Agentic DevOps and GitHub Copilot Deep-Dive]
    D3 -->|Apply Copilot across CI/CD and DevOps processes| D3A[Apply Copilot to CI/CD code review incident response and workflow automation]

    D1 -->|We want broader rollout across multiple teams| D4[GitHub Copilot Adoption and Value Realization]
    D4 -->|Drive structured adoption and measurable outcomes| D4A[Scale usage with structured adoption metrics and champions]

    E -->|What is needed to move forward at scale?| E1{What support is needed to scale?}

    E1 -->|Do leaders need clarity on value and direction?| E2[GitHub Copilot for Business Fundamentals]
    E2 -->|Align leadership on value and adoption strategy| E2A[Align on business value readiness and adoption strategy]

    E1 -->|Are there concerns around governance or security?| E3[GitHub Copilot Business Administration and Security Workshop]
    E3 -->|Set up policies controls and admin practices| E3A[Address policy telemetry license management audit logs and governance]

    E1 -->|Do teams need to understand latest capabilities?| E4[Technical Update Briefing for GitHub Copilot]
    E4 -->|Bring teams up to speed on new features| E4A[Review new features integrations best practices and security considerations]

    E1 -->|Do we need to measure impact and improve usage?| E5[Solution Optimization for GitHub Copilot]
    E5 -->|Define metrics and optimize adoption| E5A[Define productivity metrics measurement framework and optimization plan]

    %% Cross-flow transitions with guidance

    C2 -->|Once teams are comfortable, move to hands-on team scenarios| C3
    C2 -->|If teams are ready to go deeper, start building developer skills| D2

    C3 -->|After initial hands-on experience, formalize best practices| D2

    D2 -->|When teams are consistent, expand into broader workflows| D3
    D3 -->|Once advanced usage is in place, scale across teams| D4
    D4 -->|After scaling, measure and refine impact| E5

    E2 -->|After leadership alignment, address governance needs| E3
    E3 -->|Once governance is in place, enable teams further| D2
    E4 -->|After understanding new features, optimize usage| E5
    E5 -->|Use insights to improve and expand adoption| D4

